            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## One project at a time

The sidebar now shows a single project. Switch projects from the menu at the top of the sidebar, or press ⌘1 to ⌘9.

- Search still covers every project, with results grouped by project.
- Projects out of view that have something running or crashed stay listed at the bottom of the sidebar, one click away.
- Grove remembers which project you were looking at.
- Selecting a script from the menu bar switches the sidebar to its project.

## Fixes for macOS 27

- Opening a second pane no longer makes the window wider than your screen. Four panes fit in a normal window again, and you can drag the dividers to resize panes. Double-click a divider to even them out.
- In a narrow pane, the toolbar hides the usage readout and status text instead of cutting off buttons.
- App icons are back in the Open In menu.
]]></description>
